#NEXUS

[ fonseca2024a_fig2: Early dinosaur and ornithischian strict consensus, two columns joined by a connector. Internal labels: the bold node names (Pan-Aves, Pterosauromorpha, Dinosauromorpha, Dinosauria, Eusaurischia, Ornithischia, Parapredentata, Saphornithischia, Heterodontosaurinae, Genasauria, Thyreophoroidea, Eurypoda, Ankylosauria, Euankylosauria, Neornithischia, Pyrodontia, Thescelosaurinae, Marginocephalia, Euceratopsia, Hypsilophodontidae, Ornithopoda, Iguanodontia, Euiguanodontia, Dryomorpha, Styacosterna, as printed) and the legend names of numbered dots 1-12 (Lagerpetidae, Sauropodomorpha, Theropoda, Stegosauria, Parankylosauria, Orodrominae, Chaoyangsauridae, Pachycephalosauridae, Tenontosauridae, Rhabdodontoidea, Rhabdodontidae, Camptosauridae). The large names on the shaded boxes (Saurischia, Thyreophora, Ceratopsia, etc.) are not encoded. Read by eye from 2-4x crops: the hairline branches break where clade names sit across them, so the pixel listing could not be used. 170 tips, 7 polytomies (6, 6, 5, 3, 12, 7, 3 children); 37 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Random-sample case (seed 20261114). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

